    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **28 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the two new `Cp17Tests`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe owner's `locality` is a read-time derived field, matching the existing pattern for other derived owner fields (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.):\n\n1. **`Localities.java`** (new, `rest.function.common`) \u2014 the fixed city-to-region table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) with a single `of(city)` method returning the canonical region, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other/`null` city.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so it's generated onto `OwnerDto` and appears in the JSON response.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `imports = Localities.class` and a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(Localities.of(owner.getCity()))\")` so the DTO field is populated from the entity's city.\n\nThe `locality` field now surfaces on every owner response (e.g. `GET /api/owners/{id}`), reusing the same MapStruct-expression mechanism the other derived fields already use.",
